  "result": "I fixed it: shell completion now keeps `#` as part of the argument instead of dropping it and everything after it.\n\n**Cause:** completion splits the command line with `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. That function uses Python's `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. So `cli a#b c` was split as `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`.\n\n**Fix:** I added one line in `split_arg_string`, `lex.commenters = \"\"`, which turns off comment handling. The shell has already handled comments before completion runs, so a `#` that reaches this point is part of an argument.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`:\n- `\"cli a#b c\"` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`\n- `\"cli #abc\"` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"#abc\"]`\n\nBoth new cases fail without the fix and pass with it. All 67 tests in `test_parser.py` and `test_shell_completion.py` pass. Nothing is committed yet.",
